Here at thy feet, young bard, I kneel and beg you tell us how that it began;
So much has been accomplished by your works to lighten sorrow's gloom.
Many times have we laughed; many times have we shed tears as well for all things here in this world are wrought by what is good or bad on high above - a simple story, yet one worth telling again! For so long ago did I start writing about my own life experiences as if they were part of some greater scheme which made sense only now because each person has different ideas when it gets down to details like what will happen next month or year out there beyond tomorrow mornings horizon where everyone else seems contented just staying put waiting patiently until then…the whole idea behind poetry being able interpret anything that crosses our minds regardless whether we’re happy sad excited depressed ecstatic angry joyous pensive thoughtful remorseful or even feeling nothing but numbness inside ourselves sometimes can translate into words beautifully written down upon paper with care so others might read them someday perhaps years far into future time spans after death occurs. It may lead somaeone closer towards appreciating art form called ‘poetry’. But no matter how beautiful its message may be, without those feelings of personal expression it cannot exist anymore than air needs water but still requires both sources (breathing) while alive breathing living air needs liquid source moisture found within lungs through oxygen intake process).

In the city in whose dark streets every person has its own particular demon;
A place where people can walk, undisturbed by their unrelenting obsessions;
In the metropolis that consumes her inhabitants with all her power and wizardry;
The one who lives there may find redemption in another's eyes, or she must suffer under it alone (forever);
This is how they look out at each other through those windows which will never turn them into the sun--
